  "steps": [
    "The saved-scene directory loads independently of editable fields and schematic sampling. A held real reply preserves focused incomplete input. Two instances of the same definition have the same author name and distinct complete IDs. A missing saved target remains unchanged and fails Check explicitly.",
    "Choosing an instance explicitly changes only that form target. Check validates the complete animation against the catalog. Chinese, English and Japanese at 390px preserve the input/select nodes, focus, text selection, target ID and reviewed source; full identity labels and footer actions remain accessible.",
    "An injected failing transport response revokes catalog-dependent approval while preserving form values and the checked Rust schematic. Manual Check remains available and explicitly says targets are unverified. Refreshing successfully revokes that manual approval until the new directory is checked.",
    "After a real on-disk scene edit removes the selected instance, Apply performs a new authenticated directory read and rejects the stale catalog. The animation source and ordinary draft remain unchanged and the form selection is retained. The temporary scene is restored byte-for-byte before later checks.",
    "Closing with a pending real directory reply preserves the ordinary draft. Reopening starts a new catalog session; releasing the old reply cannot replace the newly selected instance or its approval.",
    "A fresh catalog is checked again at Apply, which changes only the ordinary source draft. Reopening reads that unsaved draft; Cancel retains it. Ordinary Save changes only the animation document, retaining BOM/CRLF and all scene, definition, template and registration files."
  ],
